From b6db3c9e07cdb62c636e0d67ec5066909f60cab8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bilal Ahmed <email@bilal.me>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 08:41:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat: cloud snapshot restore + provider API updates

Storage integrations updated to current provider APIs:
- alibaba: migrate OSS Signature V1 -> V4 (V1 retired for new buckets)
- backblaze/linode/ionos/upcloud storage: pin boto3 checksum config to
  when_required (providers reject boto3 >=1.36 default CRC32 headers)
- upcloud storage: drop dead region parsing from retired endpoint format
- dropbox: use refresh token for deletes (access tokens expire ~4h)
- google_drive: fix node-folder lookup recreating the folder every upload
- onedrive: fix validate() probing /drives/{user_id} instead of drive_id

Cloud snapshot integrations updated to current provider APIs:
- aws_rds: fix poll_status passing snapshot id as DB instance id; fix
  nonexistent delete_dbsnapshot call in soft_delete
- google_cloud: fix AuthorizedSession passed as requests headers at all
  call sites; fix list paging param (maxResults)
- lightsail: fix volume snapshot state check (completed, not available)
- upcloud: fix provider error body key (error_message)
- oracle: use correct SDK model constants in validate()

Add snapshot restore for all cloud providers:
- New CoreCloudRestore model + migration, restore_cloud_backup and
  poll_cloud_restore celery tasks, POST /nodes/{id}/restore_backup and
  GET /nodes/{id}/restores endpoints
- restore_snapshot/check_restore implemented for aws, aws_rds,
  digitalocean, google_cloud, hetzner, lightsail, oracle,
  ovh (ca/eu/us), upcloud and vultr: restores create a new provider
  resource from the snapshot and poll until ready
